.TH XYMOND_WEBSOCKET 8 "Version 4.3.31" "Xymon"
.SH NAME
xymond_websocket \- broadcast Xymon status changes to WebSocket clients
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "xymond_channel --channel=stachg xymond_websocket --origin=ORIGIN [options]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xymond_websocket
is a worker for the xymond status-change channel. It listens on a loopback TCP
socket, accepts same-origin WebSocket upgrades, and broadcasts each actual
status transition as JSON.
.PP
The worker retains the latest 500 transitions in memory. It sends a generation
identifier followed by the retained transitions to each new connection. The
ring and generation are process-local: restarting the worker starts with an
empty ring and does not read or write a checkpoint.
.PP
The listener should not be exposed directly. A webserver terminates HTTP or
HTTPS and proxies the Xymon Live WebSocket path to the loopback listener. The
worker rejects browser upgrades unless both the complete Origin and Host match
the configured browser-facing origin. The packaged task passes XYMONWEBHOST.
.PP
Xymon does not overwrite an existing locally managed xymon-apache.conf during
upgrade. Existing installations must merge the generated Xymon Live ProxyPass
directives into their active webserver configuration.
.SH OPTIONS
.IP "\fB\-\-origin=ORIGIN\fR"
Require this browser origin, including its http or https scheme and optional
port. This option is mandatory. Do not include a path; a trailing slash is
accepted in the configured value.
.IP "\fB\-\-listen=ADDRESS\fR"
Listen on this IPv4 address. The default is 127.0.0.1.
.IP "\fB\-\-port=PORT\fR"
Listen on this TCP port. The default is 1985. The packaged task uses
XYMONLIVEWEBSOCKETPORT from xymonserver.cfg.
.IP "\fB\-\-debug\fR"
Enable debugging output.
.SH PROTOCOL
The gateway accepts WebSocket version 13 at the path
.BR /xymonlive .
After the upgrade it sends a hello object containing the process generation,
then zero or more change objects from the in-memory ring. New change objects
are sent as transitions arrive. Each change includes the host, test, old and
new colors, transition time, sequence number, and up to 511 bytes from the
first human-readable line of the status message body. Disable and
acknowledgement actions are sent as distinct event types carrying their
comments. Idle connections receive WebSocket ping frames.
The gateway also sends heartbeat JSON objects so browsers can detect a stalled
connection even when the TCP socket remains open.
If its xymond status-change channel disappears, the gateway sends an explicit
xymond-unavailable object before closing browser connections.
Xymond also publishes a heartbeat marker every 30 seconds. If the gateway sees
no channel activity for 90 seconds, it reports xymond unavailable while keeping
the browser connection alive, and reports live again when channel activity
resumes.
.SH SEE ALSO
xymonlive.cgi(1), xymond(8), xymond_channel(8)